# Refresh UI after language change

`AppLocale::setLanguage` and `loadFromSettings` notify `LocaleNotifier` when the current language actually changes. A widget that owns a language combo must still refresh its own labels, placeholders, buttons, combo items, dialog titles, and status strings.

Do not assume a parent `languageChanged` connection will paint this widget. Call `applyUiStrings()` after `setLanguage`. If that helper writes the combo index, block its signals so `currentIndexChanged` cannot recurse.

```cpp
// BAD — locale changes; this form stays in the previous language
void GameSetupWindow::onLanguageComboChanged(int index) {
  AppLocale::setLanguage(index == 1 ? AppLocale::Language::Spanish
                                    : AppLocale::Language::English);
}

// GOOD
void GameSetupWindow::onLanguageComboChanged(int index) {
  AppLocale::setLanguage(index == 1 ? AppLocale::Language::Spanish
                                    : AppLocale::Language::English);
  QSignalBlocker languageComboBlocker(languageCombo_);
  applyUiStrings();
}
```

Keep `LocaleNotifier` subscriptions on parents for language changes that originate elsewhere.
